xterm: embed Hack Braille and make it the default font

Compile Hack Braille (Hack 3.003 plus the braille patterns U+2800..U+28FF,
regular, bold, italic and bold italic) into xterm and default faceName to
"Hack Braille" at 12 points.  The fonts are registered with fontconfig
from memory (memfd) at startup; nothing is installed.  faceName ""
still selects bitmap fonts.  License as Hack: MIT and Bitstream Vera.

Needs hack-braille-3.003/ (HackBraille-*.ttf, LICENSE.md, README,
mkhackbraille.py) unpacked into the source tree.
Apply after xterm-412-min-contrast.patch.

Commits (branch embedded-font on xterm-412):
  30df42b Embed Cascadia Mono PL and make it the default font
  d361a44 Embed Hack Braille instead of Cascadia Mono PL
  bdfa5c7 Add copyright notices to the new font embedding files

